Ported, with attribution, and otherwise left verbatim:

- System prompts: packages/core/src/session/runner/prompt/system.txt
- Provider prompts: packages/core/src/plugin/system-prompt/ (anthropic, gpt, gpt-astra, kimi, meta, trinity)
- Tool descriptions: read, write, edit, glob, grep, shell, webfetch, websearch, todowrite, patch
- Slash-command prompts: /init (initialize.txt) and /review (review.txt)
- Prompt selection in packages/core/src/plugin/optimize.ts
- Edit matching (exact match, then line-trim / curly-quote fallback)
- The `*** Begin Patch` envelope used by the patch tool
- The models.dev catalog (https://models.dev/api.json), including OpenCode Zen

A mobile addendum is appended after those prompts. It tells the model that the shell tool is a JavaScript sandbox and that there is no companion computer. The upstream prompt files are not rewritten.

This app does not vendor the OpenCode CLI, the desktop app, or any server. Model requests go from the phone to the provider API the user configures.
